@title WR-21: The Geometrization Upgrade Is A Shared Cross-Mission Dependency
@sigils [⚖/令]
@audience futon stack operators, agents, mission authors
@references [campaign-coherence/shared-standard-has-no-single-owner]
@references-extra ["Charter source and downstream evidence: futon3c/holes/campaigns/C-substrate-completion.md, chartered from WR-21 and dissolved 2026-06-03 after STANDARD-VERIFY and live E1 consumption"]
@tone foundational
@style pattern

! conclusion: Build one ground metric on substrate-2 as a shared standard beneath every mission that needs real geometry, instead of letting each mission grow another thin geometric substitute.

  + context: War Room decision WR-21 (2026-05-31). Operator: Joe. M-aif2, M-differentiable-code, M-live-geometric-stack, and E-codebase-manifold converge on the same missing primitive.

  + IF:
    Multiple missions require distance, curvature, continuity, gradients, or manifold reconstruction from the same substrate.

  + HOWEVER:
    The existing substrate-2 geometry is only a scalar T on nodes plus discrete ΔT on edges, a function painted on a graph rather than a manifold. The thin scalar field had already forked into three thin shadows, and no single mission could establish that its local substitute was adequate for all consumers.

  + THEN:
    Deprecate the thin scalar field as a target while retaining it as v0. Build a ground metric from dependency, git co-change, and semantic distance; derive Ollivier–Ricci curvature through Wasserstein distance, continuity through spectral or diffusion embedding, and manifold reconstruction from that shared base. Relate the internal Fisher–Rao geometry of the War Machine belief simplex to the external optimal-transport geometry of the codebase.

  + BECAUSE:
    Cross-mission adequacy has no single-mission owner. A shared metric contract lets each consumer depend on the same verified primitive and prevents curvature, continuity, and manifold reconstruction from diverging into incompatible local approximations.

    + evidence: C-substrate-completion was chartered directly from WR-21 after recording the three thin variants. It delivered and verified the shared metric contract, released the E1 and E2 dependencies, and dissolved on 2026-06-03 after M-aif2 consumed curvature live.
